 "best_diff": "--- initial\n+++ best\n@@ -19,17 +19,22 @@\n     (time.process_time(); more than 1.5 x the limit makes the program invalid).\n     Only the Python standard library may be used.\n \n-    Current method: next fit (open a new bin whenever the next item does not fit).\n+    Uses first-fit decreasing: process indices sorted by decreasing size and place each item\n+    in the first bin that can accommodate it; otherwise start a new bin.\n     \"\"\"\n+    indices_sorted = sorted(range(len(sizes)), key=lambda i: sizes[i], reverse=True)\n     bins = []\n-    current, load = [], 0\n-    for i, s in enumerate(sizes):\n-        if load + s > capacity:\n-            bins.append(current)\n-            current, load = [], 0\n-        current.append(i)\n-        load += s\n-    if current:\n-        bins.append(current)\n+    current_bin = []\n+    current_load = 0\n+    for idx in indices_sorted:\n+        s = sizes[idx]\n+        if current_load + s > capacity:\n+            bins.append(current_bin)\n+            current_bin = []\n+            current_load = 0\n+        current_bin.append(idx)\n+        current_load += s\n+    if current_bin:\n+        bins.append(current_bin)\n     return bins\n # OMEGA-BLOCK-END\n",
